   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the environmental conservation law, in relation to allowing the use of rifles for hunting in Ontario county; and providing for the repeal of such provisions upon expiration thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S6057",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6057-2009",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §11-0907, En Con L",
    "lawSection": "Environmental Conservation Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S6057\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act to amend the environmental conservation law, in relation to\nallowing the use of rifles for hunting in Ontario county; and\nproviding for the repeal of such provisions upon expiration thereof\n\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nThis bill would allow the hunting of deer and bear through the use of\na rifle in Ontario County south of NYS Route 20 for two years.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nOntario County has requested that they be included in those areas\nwhere sportsmen and women are able to hunt deer and bear with rifles\nsouth of NYS Route 20. Since 2005, several counties in Southern and\nCentral New York have been allowing the hunting of deer and bear with\nrifles with few if any reported incidents or other problems. With that\nsafe history, and given the rural nature of Ontario County south of\nNYS Route 20, it would seem to only make sense to now include Ontario\nCounty within these provisions as they have requested.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNew bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately.\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
